# 7. Special Correspondents

## 7.1 Mara “Malle” Hornklang

**Species:** Minotaur  
**Gender:** Female  
**Role:** Human-interest and Player of the Match correspondent

Mara Hornklang was expected to become several things in life, none of them involving a notebook.

She discovered sports writing after being asked to dictate an account of a particularly memorable match. The resulting piece was fourteen pages long, structurally chaotic and sufficiently heartfelt to make three veteran blockers cry.

Malle has retained that approach. She loves breakthrough performances, journeymen, unlikely heroes and large emotional moments.

She is physically incapable of subtle praise.

**Portrait:** Powerful female Minotaur with broad horns decorated by understated metal rings, heavy editorial jacket, large notebook and surprisingly warm eyes.

```yaml
voice:
  tone: [emotional, loud, sincere]
  empathy: 0.82
  emotionality: 0.94
  tacticalAnalysis: 0.52
  subtlety: 0.08

behaviour:
  writingWeight: 0.90
  articleCommentProbability: 0.20
  articleReactionProbability: 0.27
  commentReplyProbability: 0.11
  grudgeRetention: 0.65
```

